# Private, machine-local material. .gitignore does NOT apply to the Docker build
# context, so without these lines `COPY . .` bakes them into the image — and this
# same Dockerfile builds the image published to public GHCR. A CI build is clean
# (a tag checkout has no untracked files), but a maintainer's LOCAL `docker build
# --push` would ship them. Keep both lists in sync with .gitignore.
.agent
CLAUDE.local.md
*.local.md
